----- SOURCE CODE
@external(erlang, "one", "two")
@external(webassembly, "node:path", "basename")
pub fn basename(path: String) -> String


----- ERROR
error: Invalid WebAssembly module
  ┌─ /src/one/two.gleam:2:1
  │
2 │ @external(webassembly, "node:path", "basename")
  │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

The function `basename` has an external WebAssembly implementation in the
module `node:path`, which is neither a JavaScript module, ending in `.mjs`
or `.js`, nor a module of the environment, with a plain name like `env`.

Hint: To use another JavaScript module, write a `.mjs` module that
re-exports it.
